From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paolo Pisati <paolo.pisati@canonical.com>
Date: Fri, 3 Jul 2026 14:34:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] UBUNTU: SAUCE: media: venus: core: guard SC8280XP/SM8350
 resources behind !IRIS

Commits eff820fe8537 ("UBUNTU: SAUCE: media: venus: core: Add SM8350
resource struct") and 879843f840c5 ("UBUNTU: SAUCE: media: venus: core:
Add SC8280XP resource struct") were written against a tree predating the
venus/iris switch (8f100f5896e1 "media: qcom: venus: flip the venus/iris
switch") and were not reconciled with it during the v7.2 rebase.

The switch moved the sm8250/sm8350/sc7280 resource definitions and the
VPU_VERSION_IRIS2{,_1} enum values behind
'#if (!IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_VIDEO_QCOM_IRIS))'. However:

  - sc8280xp_res is defined outside that guard yet references the guarded
    sm8350_reg_preset, sm8250_bw_table_enc/dec and VPU_VERSION_IRIS2;
  - the sc8280xp-venus and sm8350-venus of_device_id entries are outside
    the guard yet reference sc8280xp_res / sm8350_res.

With CONFIG_VIDEO_QCOM_IRIS=y this breaks the build:

  core.c:1242: error: 'sm8350_reg_preset' undeclared here
  core.c:1244: error: 'sm8250_bw_table_enc' undeclared here
  core.c:1246: error: 'sm8250_bw_table_dec' undeclared here
  core.c:1260: error: 'VPU_VERSION_IRIS2' undeclared here
  core.c:1289: error: 'sm8350_res' undeclared here

SC8280XP and SM8350 are IRIS2-class parts handled by the iris driver, so
wrap the sc8280xp resource block and move the two of_device_id entries
inside the existing '!IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_VIDEO_QCOM_IRIS)' guard, matching
the treatment of the sc7280/sm8250 entries.

Signed-off-by: Paolo Pisati <paolo.pisati@canonical.com>
Ledger-Change: C-00168
Ledger-Origin: ubuntu@e10accb233d6be63767dbcd80a1fecf5b8fb9424
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c
index f424585aee0f..f92d2a683f62 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c
@@ -1287,6 +1287,7 @@ static const struct venus_resources qcm2290_res = {
 	.min_fw = &min_fw,
 };
 
+#if (!IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_VIDEO_QCOM_IRIS))
 static const struct freq_tbl sc8280xp_freq_table[] = {
 	{ 0, 239999999 },
 	{ 0, 338000000 },
@@ -1329,6 +1330,7 @@ static const struct venus_resources sc8280xp_res = {
 	.cp_nonpixel_size = 0x24800000,
 	.fwname = "qcom/vpu-2.0/venus.mbn",
 };
+#endif
 
 
 static const struct of_device_id venus_dt_match[] = {
@@ -1338,15 +1340,15 @@ static const struct of_device_id venus_dt_match[] = {
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,msm8998-venus", .data = &msm8998_res },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,qcm2290-venus", .data = &qcm2290_res },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sc7180-venus", .data = &sc7180_res },
-	{ .compatible = "qcom,sc8280xp-venus", .data = &sc8280xp_res },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sdm660-venus", .data = &sdm660_res },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sdm845-venus", .data = &sdm845_res },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sdm845-venus-v2", .data = &sdm845_res_v2 },
 #if (!IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_VIDEO_QCOM_IRIS))
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sc7280-venus", .data = &sc7280_res },
+	{ .compatible = "qcom,sc8280xp-venus", .data = &sc8280xp_res },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm8250-venus", .data = &sm8250_res },
-#endif
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm8350-venus", .data = &sm8350_res },
+#endif
 	{ }
 };
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, venus_dt_match);
